ce_id">ev:879c069ed129535a</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">file_name=Pump_Cavitation/CW_Pump_Cavitation_60_Load.csv; schema_type=scenario; scenario=Cooling-water pump cavitation; nominal_load=60%; severity_or_program=single load condition; header_rows=3; data_rows=5845; columns=73; anomaly_state=binary (0=pre-anomaly, 1=anomaly); notes=Pre-anomaly and anomaly segments. Compressor Filter Loss (dPf) and Turbine Back Pressure (dPex) not recorded in this run (columns present but empty).</data><data key="name">包含试验</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含试验", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e8ca5aec715faadd" source="shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7" target="shipkg:fault:999defd690d8"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_12_oily_rag</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:e3771166c08962b6</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ked rag to fall onto the hot manifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the camera monitor.</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e8cd2ef344b47d4d" source="shipkg:check:de8a5b9844ad" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d2bfff6df47b53cc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">18</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">2013 The Lessons 1. The turning gear interlock had not been included within the planned maintenance system on board and there was no record of it having been tested. 2. Control console illumination panels are vital to the safe operation of machinery and should therefore be tested regularly. If problems with visual indication or warning lamps cannot be rectified immediately, they must be repo</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e8fb5d6d9da903c6" source="shipkg:run:0024b0cf204d" target="shipkg:fault:0e24c2957173"><data key="relation">TESTS_FAULT</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:64a3e1d72c1647d2</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">file_name=AF_Clogging/AF_Clogging_60_Load.csv; schema_type=scenario; scenario=Air-filter clogging (compressor); nominal_load=60%; severity_or_program=single load condition; header_rows=3; data_rows=6819; columns=73; anomaly_state=binary (0=pre-anomaly, 1=anomaly); notes=Pre-anomaly and anomaly segments.</data><data key="name">试验故障</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "试验故障", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e9759bdb899dbec9" source="shipkg:observation:5d48f4f61abd" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:b935264465ef205c</data><data key="source_file">Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/20101612</data><data key="quote">System / engine-family case=CAT 3516C intermediate bearing EB 4; Fault or condition=Unconfirmed bearing-related warning; Detection/event reference=Vibration alert Month -2.0; maintenance event; Reference class=LTI_maintenance; LTI / warning (mo)=2.0; Warning (h)=300.0; Recommended CBM action=Vibration-only CBM; 125 h vibration interval; Included in mechanical LTI summary=yes</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e991dcc60de6485a" source="shipkg:case:551512d967af" target="shipkg:action:8076c8558f20"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a9d1c3390e834930</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">15</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">g run. 3. Check cards can be a useful aid to fault diagnosis and rectification when things get hectic. However, in this case, the need to isolate the main air cylinder when the reserve air cylinder was brought on line was not included. Consequently, the air pressure equalised at a level that was insufficient to re-engage the main engine’s clutches. Use check cards, but don’t let them stop you f</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:e9b0f37033e21813" source="shipkg:component:960fe73dbb4b" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:8e948de9b710ce4f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ond compressor (No2) and reported his actions to the senior engineer in the ECR. Immediate investigation identified that the main lubricating oil discharge pipe assembly in No1 compressor had detached, and that the bottom end bearing had overheated and failed (see figure). No1 compressor was isolated but the engineers soon noticed that the air pressure in the main air receiver was dropping. Short</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ea027a84acae7cff" source="shipkg:equipment:6cc9aa419de7" target="shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:45cb3bc7993a557f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf</data><data key="page">84</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">y’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fr</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "transmission", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ea2c70d8df227d3e" source="shipkg:faulttype:ce7933999459" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:liner_scuffing</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:ec47f7f58361e500</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2016_633_piston_rings_scuffing.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-633.pdf</data><data key="quote">to polishing and, possibly, smearing of the surface. When the liner surface is smeared, the open graphite lamel - las are closed making it difficult to keep a proper oil film. When the oil film is compromised, the cast iron piston rings, which are in contact with the cast iron liner, may generate high friction and seizures that will not recover (liner scuffing). During scuffing, the surface of the lin</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ea408031a5706e10" source="shipkg:dataset:19e52eb49467" target="shipkg:fault:ebfac27b4d41"><data key="relation">SHOWS_CONDITION</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">simulated</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a50b62c3875a33d5</data><data key="source_file">TSRF_main.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://github.com/TS-RF/TSRF</data><data key="quote">Ring-wear.csv</data><data key="name">呈现状态</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "呈现状态", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ea57d95758074a21" source="shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2" target="shipkg:action:bb1cd030e27b"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7ce8bf353caf8467</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">70</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">accident (Annex K). Carnival PLC has: • Included harmonic filters in its list of critical equipment for QM2, and has ensured that procedures exist for regular testing of their protection systems. • Developed and implemented procedures for dealing with harmonic filter imbalance alarms and entering harmonic filter rooms after an alarm has activated. • Replaced all the capacitors in QM2’s aft harmonic filter. Converteam has</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eaa4e12083f52246" source="shipkg:equipment:23fe6c4f1acc" target="shipkg:component:d16e663b1271"><data key="relation">HAS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:470e8782d7a79377</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">t in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of the back pressure valve (PSV3) becoming jammed in the closed position. The reason for the temporary increase in the starboard main engine load to 100% and corresponding increase in turbocharger rpm has not been det</data><data key="name">包含部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eaa95f7f563acf08" source="shipkg:check:64ccf3c3f401" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:aee93ed7c1866eb1</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">id not fully understand the vessel’s propulsion control system and had not routinely tested their back-up and emergency controls. Regular testing of back-up and emergency control systems, and the conduct of machinery breakdown drills, provide the most effective method of ensuring the crew fully understand their ship’s systems and are best prepared to respond in an emergency. Figure 3: Damage to linkspan, mooring</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ead8467351a90af8" source="shipkg:case:00057f56fe39" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">wight_sky_me_2017</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:19d0b2283f62b511</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf</data><data key="quote">examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eb00e74b105c9e6b" source="shipkg:condition:4dcab8c954bb" target="shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad"><data key="relation">LIMITS_DETECTION_OF</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7058770c39736963</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">30</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">24 the valves and their refitting was deemed an unnecessary measure. However, the oil sampling programme had not identified the wear in the back pressure valve as it had, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by</data><data key="name">妨碍发现</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "妨碍发现", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eb171c3e43f0cd6e" source="shipkg:vessel:32aaec3208ad" target="shipkg:vesseltype:1831d47f0525"><data key="relation">OF_VESSEL_TYPE</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_12_oily_rag</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7293e870a8d5467f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">40</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines</data><data key="name">船型为</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "船型为", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eb3433ff68f18d3e" source="shipkg:condition:bdbca1b8295e" target="shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:6522054ba5597880</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">16</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control panel, showed that the turning gear was in, this was poorly illuminated and was not seen by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage t</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "transmission", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eba8a51a21135135" source="shipkg:consequence:5c4ffe048cb7" target="shipkg:consequence:35c015f940ee"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_05_cpp_backup</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d11a787d7d142f9d</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">19</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">a speed of about 7 knots and made heavy contact with the concrete berth (Figure 3). Almost immediately, bilge alarms, indicating water ingress into the vessel’s forward spaces, began to sound. The pitch on both propellers was brought to zero but the main engines were kept running. The bridge team made safety announcements to the passengers, alerted the port authorities and requested tug assistance. The</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ec20706ed9eea2ce" source="shipkg:faulttype:660e09f63773" target="shipkg:source:2be14752326a"><data key="relation">DOCUMENTED_BY</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:coolant_blockage</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:1ac13d5b81e13593</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf</data><data key="quote">der head. The damages are often a result of corrosion, restrictions in or blocking of the cooling water flow, which are caused by deposits of limescale and/or rust. In general corrosion may result in leakages and thereby re - duce the lifetime and safety of the engine components. Lime- scale as well as rust deposits will reduce the heat transfer and may result in thermal overload of the com</data><data key="name">记载于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "记载于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ec264eeb7766cd8b" source="shipkg:equipment:5d25f4bda048" target="shipkg:component:960fe73dbb4b"><data key="relation">HAS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:8e948de9b710ce4f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ond compressor (No2) and reported his actions to the senior engineer in the ECR. Immediate investigation identified that the main lubricating oil discharge pipe assembly in No1 compressor had detached, and that the bottom end bearing had overheated and failed (see figure). No1 compressor was isolated but the engineers soon noticed that the air pressure in the main air receiver was dropping. Short</data><data key="name">包含部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ec32b6f345cc361f" source="shipkg:dataset:710ea13e53ac" target="shipkg:observation:f5d747e68b69"><data key="relation">HAS_CASE</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:596b2f398d646f0b</data><data key="source_file">Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/20101612</data><data key="quote">System / engine-family case=CAT C7 shaftline reductor / CAT C7 case A; Fault or condition=Structural looseness; Detection/event reference=Vibration alert Month -3.5; operational failure/gearbox repair; Reference class=LTI_operational; LTI / warning (mo)=3.5; Warning (h)=525.0; Recommended CBM action=Vibration-only CBM; 125 h vibration interval; Included in mechanical LTI summary=yes</data><data key="name">包含案例</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含案例", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ec34500d561a3beb" source="shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5" target="shipkg:action:b1b278b9bbdd"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:c7e7236b07b0d8d2</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf</data><data key="page">53</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality</data><data key="quote">obal GmbH &amp; Co. KG has: ● Updated the SISHIp eSiPods software and corrected the operators’ manual. ● Updated the PCS to include a revised WLS sequence activation that allows the crew to intervene and prevent the SISHIp eSiPODs parking at 90° to the vessel’s heading. ● Increased the SISHIp eSiPODs overspeed activation point following a mechanical evaluation of the systems. ● Improved the position of the SISHIp eSiPODs bilg</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ec95dc1fa6992435" source="shipkg:dataset:1ceeb4cad6d8" target="shipkg:run:6c075208cdc0"><data key="relation">HAS_RUN</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9de953977942cbdf</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">file_name=Turbine_Degradation/Turbine_Degradation_40_Load.csv; schema_type=scenario; scenario=Turbine degradation; nominal_load=40%; severity_or_program=single load condition; header_rows=3; data_rows=6397; columns=73; anomaly_state=binary (0=pre-anomaly, 1=anomaly); notes=Pre-anomaly and anomaly segments.</data><data key="name">包含试验</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含试验", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eca2ebb20a238b2d" source="shipkg:action:bb1cd030e27b" target="shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b"><data key="relation">ADDRESSES</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7ce8bf353caf8467</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">70</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">accident (Annex K). Carnival PLC has: • Included harmonic filters in its list of critical equipment for QM2, and has ensured that procedures exist for regular testing of their protection systems. • Developed and implemented procedures for dealing with harmonic filter imbalance alarms and entering harmonic filter rooms after an alarm has activated. • Replaced all the capacitors in QM2’s aft harmonic filter. Converteam has</data><data key="name">应对</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "应对", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ecbb3b0b3b413ff1" source="shipkg:consequence:2597a77f75b3" target="shipkg:consequence:ec261d7a91d6"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_09_cpp_response</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:085bb3fe51ea11cc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">head. Despite placing the pitch control to full astern, the CPP did not respond in time and the vessel’s bow struck the quay. The bulbous bow was holed, but fortunately the damage was above the waterline (Figure 1). The subsequent investigation identified that the vessel had a history of sluggish astern response. However, the crew had accepted this as a ‘characteristic’ of the v</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ecd21828868f7b9d" source="shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9" target="shipkg:consequence:4016217446bf"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">kommandor_susan_dg1_2025</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:390711bc162bb6ce</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan</data><data key="quote">r Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propulsion and began drifting eastwards. Attempts to deploy anchors were unsuccessful because the anchor winches required electrical power t</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ed0db675da67eb16" source="shipkg:faulttype:3353dce7f4ad" target="shipkg:cause:7009e2343511"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:bearing_seizure</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0523deba67297b7c</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2013_569_bearing_wear_monitoring.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2013-569.pdf</data><data key="quote">C A main bearing damage was recently experienced on an MAN B&amp;W S-MC-C main engine of medium bore size. The damage was caused by a sudden ingress of foreign matter into the bearing via the lubricating oil system, and it devel - oped rapidly into a bearing seizure. The engine was equipped with a bearing wear monitoring (BWM) system as recommended by MAN Diesel &amp; Turbo (MDT). However, for rea</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ed4a27464a4be699" source="shipkg:equipment:5ed28aa334b7" target="shipkg:component:1333df9ac9f2"><data key="relation">HAS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_05_missing_filter</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:82256a9ee8fd56dd</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">d main bearing journals; overheating of the bedplate at the main bearing housings; overheating of the piston connecting rods; the seizure of several pistons (Figure 2); failure of the camshaft and turbo charger bearings, and metallic debris throughout the lubricating oil system. The damage sustained necessitated an engine rebuild and the replacement of the bedplate and crankshaft. A</data><data key="name">包含部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ed7bbec95e1a060d" source="shipkg:fault:8969204ea965" target="shipkg:fault:401ffd7724bc"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_05_missing_filter</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0fb80ad604213aad</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and overheating to other bearings and to the pistons. The engine daily logs referred to oil filter cartridge changes only prior to the repair to the oil pumps. They also showed that the pressure reading on the differential pressure gauge for the</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ed933a1ae04c11c1" source="shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2" target="shipkg:check:5a2af85dcbf4"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:38d40fe90e8b2dbf</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">69</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">when there are no alternative or back-up systems, must fail safe. They should also be tested at regular intervals to verify that all the sub-components in the system are functional. [2.4.5] 7 . Awareness of arc-flash hazards needs to be significantly increased throughout the marine industry, so that designers, builders, owners, operators and engineers understand the hazard, risks and the potential risk redu</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ed9e4e61ea266b36" source="shipkg:faulttype:6456485708ad" target="shipkg:source:44dc69861c93"><data key="relation">DOCUMENTED_BY</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:46c70849c9c28abc</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN039_marine_shaft_generators.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-039_C-Marine-Shaft-Generators.pdf</data><data key="quote">When the shaft generator is aligned with the gearbox drive shaft, the ships design engineer must take great care to allow for the thermal expansion of the hot gearbox, which may well expand and lift the shaft centre line by &lt; 1 mm. If the alignment is not accurate, then excessive vibration is likely to damage the shaft generator. There can also be lots of generator damaging vibration when the</data><data key="name">记载于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "记载于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:edb07dad430e24d4" source="shipkg:case:597875e258c6" target="shipkg:symptom:fa4424a6b543"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_05_cpp_backup</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:b0c29f0e315a7acd</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">19</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">continued towards the port. However, a few minutes later the engineers in the engine control room noticed that the starboard CPP back-up control system indicator lamp was illuminated on their console. Having not seen this before, they discussed its significance before deciding to take no immediate action. As the vessel entered the port the master reduced speed by decreasing the pitch settings on the port and</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:edbb713d08d8dd44" source="shipkg:faulttype:84e503bec36b" target="shipkg:fault:216400f082cf"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:shaft_torsional</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:5cf0da035bedd926</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN035_fault_protection.pdf</data><data key="page">5</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-035_B-Overload-and-Fault-Protection.pdf</data><data key="quote">ic energy, identified by electrical engineers as inertia constant (H). Obviously, the coupling will be subjected to some level of transient peak torque demand during the time zero up to steady state condition and the 'typical' level considered by responsible mechanical engineers is 12 times rated torque. It should not be forgotten that the most arduous conditions for generating mechani</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ee29e9d5aa94c5ec" source="shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5" target="shipkg:fault:c830e7992f26"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:5d3cde311b090a6a</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf</data><data key="page">42</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality</data><data key="quote">e rpm of each pod’s propulsion motor very rapidly increased and exceeded the preset overspeed limitation. The pod’s PCS therefore automatically tripped the power to its motor to prevent it being damaged. Spirit of Discovery’s engineers could likely have quickly reset the port and starboard motors and restored the vessel’s propulsion had the propulsion motor overspeed trips been the only issue. However</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ee3a3fd7da059efd" source="shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3" target="shipkg:condition:4dcab8c954bb"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7058770c39736963</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">30</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">24 the valves and their refitting was deemed an unnecessary measure. However, the oil sampling programme had not identified the wear in the back pressure valve as it had, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eec6461f4fd0dde2" source="shipkg:check:52bfc5553a79" target="shipkg:cause:3667d8d2e0ca"><data key="relation">CHECKS</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_09_cpp_response</data><data key="certainty">derived_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:88dffcc589cf9235</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">y to bring the vessel back under control before it struck the quay. It was also revealed during the investigation that the system parameters for astern pitch control had been incorrectly set during the commissioning of the propulsion system when the vessel was delivered from the yard. The Lessons 1. If you are expected to manoeuvre a vessel, you should make every effort to familiarise yourself with the controls at yo</data><data key="name">检查</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "检查", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eed5662c75c14263" source="shipkg:case:597875e258c6" target="shipkg:fault:f078b5a27275"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_05_cpp_backup</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4812bf9684b2b7ad</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">14 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 The Lessons 1. Ergonomically, the layout of the bridge console was not well designed. The close proximity of the safety-critical propulsion control buttons and the similar looking everyday use dimmer buttons, increased the likelihood of the type of human error seen in this case. There is always a risk that watchkeepers and equipment operators will inadvertently press the wrong butto</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eefb148231b37a54" source="shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3" target="shipkg:condition:4fe499c68172"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a761595279b52f7c</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">ey need to be checked to ensure they continue to function correctly. However, in the case of Pride of Canterbury these valves had never been tested or inspected since the ship was constructed 23 years previously. The LIPS CPP system manual provided some maintenance instructions, including annual testing of pressure safety valve (PSV1) and the back pressure valve (PSV3). However, how this</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:eefedd80cdcdbdd0" source="shipkg:fault:216400f082cf" target="shipkg:condition:1500802ee98b"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:shaft_torsional</data><data key="certainty">guidance</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:5cf0da035bedd926</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN035_fault_protection.pdf</data><data key="page">5</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-035_B-Overload-and-Fault-Protection.pdf</data><data key="quote">ic energy, identified by electrical engineers as inertia constant (H). Obviously, the coupling will be subjected to some level of transient peak torque demand during the time zero up to steady state condition and the 'typical' level considered by responsible mechanical engineers is 12 times rated torque. It should not be forgotten that the most arduous conditions for generating mechani</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"context_id": "knowledge:shaft_torsional", "knowledge_layer": "reference", "data_origin": "manufacturer_guidance", "applicability": "内燃机-发电机传动链一般机理；证据支持扭振导致失效风险及电气故障转矩冲击，但未建立某大型船主轴联轴器断裂的已证实事故链。", "coupling_domains": "热-机-电", "name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:efb389cfdce36b21" source="shipkg:case:551512d967af" target="shipkg:consequence:fd1e977000c3"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7009d03f4c6f89d9</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">15</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ge the clutches. Although the starboard anchor was let go in an attempt to reduce the speed of approach, this did not prevent the ferry’s bow hitting her berth at a speed of 2.5kts and causing minor damage. Shortly after the impact, the engineers successfully re-engaged the port main engine clutch and the vessel was able to berth safely alongside, assisted by harbour tugs. Subsequent investigation identifie</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f019e5835fab2c46" source="shipkg:run:c2058b46e618" target="shipkg:condition:103a0ae5358b"><data key="relation">AT_LOAD</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4369bc44687256ab</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">file_name=AC_Fouling/AC_Fouling_85_Load.csv; schema_type=scenario; scenario=Air-cooler fouling; nominal_load=85%; severity_or_program=single load condition; header_rows=3; data_rows=5801; columns=73; anomaly_state=binary (0=pre-anomaly, 1=anomaly); notes=Pre-anomaly and anomaly segments. Compressor Filter Loss (dPf) and Turbine Back Pressure (dPex) not recorded in this run (columns present but empty).</data><data key="name">负载为</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "负载为", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f0265b7c7608e004" source="shipkg:condition:8012db626950" target="shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:3b167c1e7ff25a89</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf</data><data key="quote">-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. The engine manufacturer’s recommended fuel system modification had been fitted to the external fuel system of just one of Stena Europe’s four main engines. The opportunity to fit</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "fuel_air", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f075c9fecca3fcf0" source="shipkg:fault:7dd3cdd4fe58" target="shipkg:faulttype:6dbd0d51366c"><data key="relation">INSTANCE_OF</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:bearing_electrical_erosion</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0f7534e3f93d98e3</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf</data><data key="quote">porting bearings, consequently any resulting current flow will pass across the rolling element of the bearings, and will initiate electrical erosion of the bearing materials, eventually reducing the low friction expectation of the bearing. It is possible for a single bearing alternator to suffer from shaft bearing currents, but here the current flow path at the drive end of the alternator’s shaft mus</data><data key="name">归入故障类别</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_basis": "人工审核术语分类；不是由该文献证明所有实例根因相同", "name": "归入故障类别", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f08a562db82c3f55" source="shipkg:faulttype:8a35cec932af" target="shipkg:fault:655f841ec7d0"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:damper_failure</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:71b1d838f3e59389</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2017_654_torsional_damper.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2017-654.pdf</data><data key="quote">oil - r educed lube oil supply - c ontaminated lube oil leading to carbon built up internal the damper b y the centrifugal forces will reduce the service life of the torsional vibration damper and may lead to failure before reaching the mentioned operation limits. Indications of a failing torsional vibration damper could be abnormal noise from the torsional vibration damper or any chan</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f08fa036f145759a" source="shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b" target="shipkg:fault:5737f3610967"><data key="relation">LIMITS_DETECTION_OF</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:ab39293c5f3260fc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">64</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">ious problems. 2.4.5 Current imbalance detection system The capacitor exploded because the inoperative imbalance detection system could not identify the deterioration of the capacitors. The failure of the imbalance system’s current transformer remained undetected for what could have been several years. It is certain that this system was not working in 2008 when Converteam detected two defective capacitors durin</data><data key="name">妨碍发现</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "妨碍发现", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f1537cdb6f539138" source="shipkg:faulttype:40cb53a64e31" target="shipkg:check:e3171f6b59e1"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:winding_insulation</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0e3fac9dc3cdbd8f</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN040_winding_insulation.pdf</data><data key="page">6</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-040_E-Winding-Insulation-System.pdf</data><data key="quote">ce and understanding about the risk of operation of the alternator’s insulation system is required, then the next test would be a Polarization Index - PI Test. The alternator's Insulation Resistance (IR), along with many other critical factors, will have been measured during the STAMFORD | AvK factory processes of manufacture, assembly and test. The alternator will have been</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f1548e829e0af365" source="shipkg:case:537a034e93e3" target="shipkg:equipment:38482b664e19"><data key="relation">HAS_EQUIPMENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_03_turning_gear</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:b840391c6c40b9b8</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">16</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator</data><data key="name">涉及设备</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及设备", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f16e7ed6126a5ae7" source="shipkg:fault:5f59e6b3ca42" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9094aa614ec060db</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf</data><data key="quote">ntrolled environment and transferring it complete into the engine room would have reduced the likelihood of debris ingress. • The engine was not fitted with a wear detector, so there was no means of receiving a warning before the engine failed. • The essential services switchboard aft circuit breaker had been left in manual mode, resulting in the loss of power to critical equipment, including the fixed fire-fighting system. ACTION TAKEN Wightli</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f1855f0334a94c6a" source="shipkg:fault:dd6aba2caf5a" target="shipkg:fault:562580f2bf5a"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:b1d5068e305409aa</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">recommendations to prevent similar accidents occurring in the future. 2.2 CAUSE OF THE FIRE The fire was initiated following the spray of hydraulic oil, from a ruptured pipework joint in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of the back pressure valve (PSV3) becoming jammed in</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f1c220f7c37e066a" source="shipkg:fault:675217222811" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:2cdda8701b9f350e</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2017_20_Hebrides_CPP_coupling.pdf</data><data key="page">30</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/59b7ab1c40f0b61231e71a54/MAIBInvReport20_2017.pdf</data><data key="quote">CONTROL FAILURE MECHANISM It is evident from the inspection carried out by Hebrides’s engineers shortly after the accident, that control of the ferry’s port CPP was lost due to a mechanical failure within the linear servomotor actuator sited on the port gearbox (Figure 6). The setscrew used to secure one half of the jaw coupling to the stepper motor ‘D’ shaped shaft had backed off from the shaft’</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f1e601e66751d624" source="shipkg:run:bd1a1e06b4eb" target="shipkg:condition:df365e2b0777"><data key="relation">AT_LOAD</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:879c069ed129535a</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">file_name=Pump_Cavitation/CW_Pump_Cavitation_60_Load.csv; schema_type=scenario; scenario=Cooling-water pump cavitation; nominal_load=60%; severity_or_program=single load condition; header_rows=3; data_rows=5845; columns=73; anomaly_state=binary (0=pre-anomaly, 1=anomaly); notes=Pre-anomaly and anomaly segments. Compressor Filter Loss (dPf) and Turbine Back Pressure (dPex) not recorded in this run (columns present but empty).</data><data key="name">负载为</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "负载为", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f21af884f7354745" source="shipkg:action:84a87c035a24" target="shipkg:condition:b290b6459200"><data key="relation">ADDRESSES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_14_sea_valve</data><data key="certainty">reported_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d1a2571c248baad4</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">e was safely released from the suction side of the pump by using the bleed nut on the suction strainer. • Ensuring that the inlet flange was split in a controlled manner with a number of loosened bolts still in situ to enable them to be re-tightened in the event of the isolating valve not holding. 2. The crew’s response to the flooding was ineffective because they were not prepared for the emerge</data><data key="name">应对</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "应对", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f2ca87dce41f253c" source="shipkg:check:e53578d74732" target="shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9282652d0f980004</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf</data><data key="page">3</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf</data><data key="quote">ontent ≤50 mg/l ≤50 mg/l 2) Fig. 3: Rust and limescale blocks the cooling water bores (valve seat removed from cylinder head) The quality of the freshwater must be checked using the MAN Diesel &amp; Turbo water testing kit or a similar test kit pro - vided by the manufacturer. The requirements to freshwater quality are stated in Table 1. Treatment and periodical checks of the cooling water W hen distil</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "cooling", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f322909ce717c0d3" source="shipkg:fault:d26785dacafa" target="shipkg:fault:5bc176965c58"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_08_generator_oil</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a36fbb3ebb9e478c</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">26</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">t unlagged following its overhaul during the recent dry dock (Figure 2b). This was hidden from view by the exhaust casing. • Fine oil spray ignited when it came into contact with the hot exhaust casing. Figure 1: Location of the generator with the loose oil plug and the adjacent generator with the uninsulated section of the exhaust piping</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f331bb2d23d88bfe" source="shipkg:dataset:1ceeb4cad6d8" target="shipkg:sensor:366f77564e58"><data key="relation">HAS_CHANNEL</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:1fe44331fadb665a</data><data key="source_file">Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/19857425</data><data key="quote">full_name=No.1 Exh.Gas Temp.; symbol=T1; unit=°C; dtype=number; in_reference=TRUE; in_scenario_files=TRUE; category=temperature</data><data key="name">包含测点</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含测点", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f34138c6e0145787" source="shipkg:condition:be80fb98e414" target="shipkg:fault:3dabb05debb4"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:c8e14e20edb4d870</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">15</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">, the need to isolate the main air cylinder when the reserve air cylinder was brought on line was not included. Consequently, the air pressure equalised at a level that was insufficient to re-engage the main engine’s clutches. Use check cards, but don’t let them stop you from thinking on your feet as well. In the engine room, the reserve compressed air cylinder was opened but there was still insufficient air pre</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f369442f930591a9" source="shipkg:fault:562580f2bf5a" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:45f3ae7b802f6792</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">he accident as a basis for making recommendations to prevent similar accidents occurring in the future. 2.2 CAUSE OF THE FIRE The fire was initiated following the spray of hydraulic oil, from a ruptured pipework joint in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of t</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f3894185e054e017" source="shipkg:check:3b1fdbe04792" target="shipkg:fault:f2f9d4b10a0b"><data key="relation">CHECKS</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_08_generator_oil</data><data key="certainty">reported_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7732c1387876e1fb</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">28</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">s on the engines exceed acceptable limits. Overall vibration velocity can be measured with very simple instruments. If excessive, frequency analysis of the vibration waveform can often identify the root cause of excessive vibration levels. Figure 3: Example of a thermal image showing ‘hot spots’ on uninsulated sections of the exhaust system</data><data key="name">检查</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "检查", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f44931e0d75b1336" source="shipkg:fault:a20cef558a0a" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:45cb3bc7993a557f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf</data><data key="page">84</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">y’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fr</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f45e0d237e7a3e57" source="shipkg:fault:73da5c52ce5d" target="shipkg:fault:c8fa85d36573"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:90e6711ec8bfcb6f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">13</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour sprayed out, igniting and creating the likely conditions for an arc-flash to occur between the 1 1000 volt bus bars that fed power to the aft HF . A current imbalance detection system, which was the only</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f4672d81488003a7" source="shipkg:equipment:361590fc68c0" target="shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:2180f44fb45d636d</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ssel. Are you prepared for a flooding emergency? 3. Examination of the isolating valve following the accident identified that the valve actuator had been defective, giving an impression that the valve was fully closed when it was not. Although there was a visual indicator located on the side of the actuator, this was not checked to confirm that the valve was closed prior to removal of the f</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "cooling", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f46de1d1d512d556" source="shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56" target="shipkg:condition:52a5771f68ca"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_08_generator_oil</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:59a2040fb754c1d5</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">28</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">21 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 The Lessons 1. Unlagged sections of exhaust piping will radiate heat to the protective casing, causing it to attain temperatures sufficient to ignite an oil or fuel spray. 2. These temperatures are not visible to the eye unless the surface is glowing. However, a thermal image will immediately identify unlagged sections (F</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f4c38529fcb51c1f" source="shipkg:fault:74505aa1776a" target="shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:44f19b4f5b32f488</data><data key="source_file">Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://zenodo.org/records/20101612</data><data key="quote">System / engine-family case=CAT 3516C coupling EB 1; Fault or condition=Coupling resonance; Detection/event reference=Vibration alert Month -2.0; maintenance event; Reference class=LTI_maintenance; LTI / warning (mo)=2.0; Warning (h)=300.0; Recommended CBM action=Vibration-led CBM; 125 h vibration / 500 h oil; Included in mechanical LTI summary=yes</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "transmission", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f4e393236cdd2029" source="shipkg:faulttype:40cb53a64e31" target="shipkg:fault:8b8846e83caf"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:winding_insulation</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:454c2c34e07b2395</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN035_fault_protection.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-035_B-Overload-and-Fault-Protection.pdf</data><data key="quote">e within the graphically displayed current against time, in order to avoid initiating permanent damage, which would result in the thermal degradation of the alternator’s insulation system. The disconnect times are achieved by the engineer responsible for selecting a circuit breaker, which has the appropriate adjustable tripping characteristics that can be set to ensure complia</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f505f5cce7847083" source="shipkg:fault:999defd690d8" target="shipkg:component:26867a3d02f0"><data key="relation">AFFECTS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_12_oily_rag</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:188654e8f7b787d6</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ked rag to fall onto the hot manifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the ca</data><data key="name">影响部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "影响部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5466def9fbd982a" source="shipkg:condition:8012db626950" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:3b167c1e7ff25a89</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf</data><data key="quote">-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. The engine manufacturer’s recommended fuel system modification had been fitted to the external fuel system of just one of Stena Europe’s four main engines. The opportunity to fit</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5554490157ed0c6" source="shipkg:fault:323fee48e778" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:8b5ccc7bfc9235d4</data><data key="source_file">TSRF_main.zip</data><data key="page" /><data key="source_url">https://github.com/TS-RF/TSRF</data><data key="quote">Ring-adhesion.csv</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5679f933af5dd6a" source="shipkg:component:e0a03cf176fe" target="shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:861eb8fbe47cd585</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf</data><data key="quote">f pressurised fuel. The fuel sprayed onto the exposed exhaust manifold that was operating at a temperature exceeding 220°C when a screw in a two-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. Th</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "fuel_air", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5a05d14308ae52a" source="shipkg:case:9792cd36162e" target="shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">windcat8_port_engine_2017</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf</data><data key="quote">and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5b76f3c5a125c98" source="shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b" target="shipkg:action:84a87c035a24"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_14_sea_valve</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d1a2571c248baad4</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">e was safely released from the suction side of the pump by using the bleed nut on the suction strainer. • Ensuring that the inlet flange was split in a controlled manner with a number of loosened bolts still in situ to enable them to be re-tightened in the event of the isolating valve not holding. 2. The crew’s response to the flooding was ineffective because they were not prepared for the emerge</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f5f7e253a9fb05b7" source="shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b" target="shipkg:fault:db9b4536b139"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_14_sea_valve</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:e8101941c0ddc6d2</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ng emergency? 3. Examination of the isolating valve following the accident identified that the valve actuator had been defective, giving an impression that the valve was fully closed when it was not. Although there was a visual indicator located on the side of the actuator, this was not checked to confirm that the valve was closed prior to removal of the flange bolts. The actuator had previously been repaired. However, the c</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f609ab43aaccb8c6" source="shipkg:action:84a87c035a24" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d1a2571c248baad4</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">41</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">e was safely released from the suction side of the pump by using the bleed nut on the suction strainer. • Ensuring that the inlet flange was split in a controlled manner with a number of loosened bolts still in situ to enable them to be re-tightened in the event of the isolating valve not holding. 2. The crew’s response to the flooding was ineffective because they were not prepared for the emerge</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f666dae6f01177ac" source="shipkg:case:adf367a46f33" target="shipkg:cause:8a2abf94d478"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">wight_sky_me2_2018</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:f586cbe874297cd1</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf</data><data key="page">84</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silica sand and other abrasive particles embedded in the main bearing shells, engine misalignment, high levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Vol</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f6980acf5b577143" source="shipkg:fault:ce4fe75e21d8" target="shipkg:fault:4865d7c855d8"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_05_missing_filter</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:76540dbe3ce4a2dc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">engine was allowed to cool, the crankcase doors were removed; several crankshaft bearings were severely damaged (Figure 1) which prevented the engine from further operation. The vessel was towed to the nearest available port for further assessment. Subsequent investigation by the engine manufacturer determined that the damage included: the failure of all crankshaft main and crankpin bearings; the di</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f6d4787cdc819a2b" source="shipkg:equipment:5ed28aa334b7" target="shipkg:component:67b7bcd7344e"><data key="relation">HAS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_05_missing_filter</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:df67722cb172233f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">filter cartridge in the on-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and overheating to other bearings and to the pistons. The engine daily logs referred to oil filter cartridge changes only prior to the re</data><data key="name">包含部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f723bbcf2a7901a6" source="shipkg:fault:0ad9453d012b" target="shipkg:faulttype:f8ea1aa17718"><data key="relation">INSTANCE_OF</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:cooling_cavitation</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:fbe07737c9447c24</data><data key="source_file">MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf</data><data key="page">11</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf</data><data key="quote">d fuel oil consumption. – A flow which is too low may cause local boiling on the water side inside the scavenge air cooler, which may lead to cavitation in the cooling water pipes. – The stated max. scavenge air temperature values given in the technical file may be exceeded, and the engine may thereby not fulfil the Tier II NO X requirements. On this basis, a system has to be established that maintains a c</data><data key="name">归入故障类别</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_basis": "人工审核术语分类；不是由该文献证明所有实例根因相同", "name": "归入故障类别", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f76de38e7d57e6dc" source="shipkg:faulttype:8a35cec932af" target="shipkg:source:40e44500f25e"><data key="relation">DOCUMENTED_BY</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:damper_failure</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:71b1d838f3e59389</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2017_654_torsional_damper.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2017-654.pdf</data><data key="quote">oil - r educed lube oil supply - c ontaminated lube oil leading to carbon built up internal the damper b y the centrifugal forces will reduce the service life of the torsional vibration damper and may lead to failure before reaching the mentioned operation limits. Indications of a failing torsional vibration damper could be abnormal noise from the torsional vibration damper or any chan</data><data key="name">记载于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "记载于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f7d3c136149f9f3e" source="shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2" target="shipkg:source:a4b58f363149"><data key="relation">DOCUMENTED_BY</data><data key="case_id">finlandia_seaways_me_2018</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">9</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured</data><data key="quote">ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr</data><data key="name">记载于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "记载于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f7e2453fe0a220b2" source="shipkg:faulttype:8a35cec932af" target="shipkg:condition:212a684d37a2"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:damper_failure</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:66303eda9ce85d8c</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2017_654_torsional_damper.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2017-654.pdf</data><data key="quote">ses which inevitably lead to wear and tear on the torsional vibration damper. Unfavorable operating conditions such as: - e ngine over-speed - s hocks caused by hydraulic locks in engine cylinders - w ater in the lube oil - r educed lube oil supply - c ontaminated lube oil leading to carbon built up internal the damper b y the centrifugal forces will reduce the servic</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f7f3e6ed5fcb1562" source="shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5" target="shipkg:consequence:7de07882b364"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a61057fac0fe1035</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf</data><data key="page">51</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality</data><data key="quote">e vessel. [2.3.1] 3. The loss of control was exacerbated by the initiation of the pod’s water leakage stop sequence, which led to both pods being parked at 90° to the vessel’s heading. This caused the vessel to lose steerage, its bow to swing to port and its motion to become even more severe. [2.3.1] 4. The vessel’s propulsion control system was unable to prevent the loss of propulsion when its movement was wi</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f822c98b6b4fd479" source="shipkg:fault:aba0717d72a0" target="shipkg:fault:8969204ea965"><data key="relation">LEADS_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_05_missing_filter</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:09940c64e5709cec</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">n-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and overheating to other bearings and to the pistons. The engine daily logs referred to oil filter cartridge changes only prior to the repair to the oil pumps. They also showed that the pressure rea</data><data key="name">导致</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "导致", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f8708991db8070bf" source="shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_12_oily_rag</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7293e870a8d5467f</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">40</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f88ba84487c8e409" source="shipkg:check:313a552b87bf" target="shipkg:cause:29f8307f5eed"><data key="relation">CHECKS</data><data key="case_id">finlandia_seaways_me_2018</data><data key="certainty">derived_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:33782f93bde6d8a1</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">56</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured</data><data key="quote">d a competent fitter to undertake the specific task of removing the piston pin bushes at its workshops in Klaipeda. Despite this, seven of the intact 11 small ends removed from Finlandia Seaways’ engine were found to have notch damage on the internal surfaces of their small end eyes. Three of Botnia Seaways’ small ends had similar damage and three had evidence of localised heat damage. Although the technical investigations did not identify when the damage had</data><data key="name">检查</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "检查", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f8a997fd212eac55" source="shipkg:faulttype:bff048b48ff1" target="shipkg:source:44dc69861c93"><data key="relation">DOCUMENTED_BY</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:generator_bearing_wear</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:e409b2a83322445c</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN039_marine_shaft_generators.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-039_C-Marine-Shaft-Generators.pdf</data><data key="quote">at many different speeds and for much of this time unexcited, the ships maintenance schedule should include clear guidance about bearing regreasing instructions. It is recommended that the shaft generator is fitted with re- greasable bearings, which should be specified at time of order. When the shaft generator is aligned with the gearbox drive shaft, the ships design engineer must take</data><data key="name">记载于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "记载于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f91e30b569a1ffe4" source="shipkg:cause:0c02674d6024" target="shipkg:fault:2c644dcfc770"><data key="relation">CONTRIBUTED_TO</data><data key="case_id">kommandor_susan_dg1_2025</data><data key="certainty">probable</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:5f282b514e870587</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">5</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan</data><data key="quote">oot cause is failure of connecting rod bearing number five. The excessive wear on the other connecting rod bearings show that the most likely root cause for the bearing failure is weak bonding of the copper layer. Evidence of weak material bonding was found in several bearings (Figure 4). Figure 3: Comparison between genuine OEM (left) and CTP bottom end bearings (right) Image courtesy of Pon Power</data><data key="name">促成</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "促成", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f95f6bbe851a6ae8" source="shipkg:condition:133adfa97595" target="shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:6d6d03a1efd0d418</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">60</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ated as designed, with no one present in the wheelhouse to either see or hear it, it was not detected in time to save the vessel. Never leave the wheelhouse unmanned when underway; doing so is in contravention of the COLREGs and puts you and your vessel at risk. 2. The crew were instructed to enter the accommodation to collect lifejackets in preparation for abandoning the vessel, but instead took personal</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "cooling", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f969f426eeb89319" source="shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2" target="shipkg:consequence:4016217446bf"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:488cfef2b71e970c</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">13</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">thin the aft HF at the time of the accident caused general instability in the electrical network which could not be contained and led to the generators shutting down. Lloyd’s Register (Europe, Middle East and Asia) (LR) has been recommended to take forward proposals to the International Association of Classification Societies to: • Establish a requirement for all new vessels fitted with harmo</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:f9868eeca0e99d78" source="shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3" target="shipkg:check:b6e1865763c1"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">pride_can_cpp_2014</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:ccd29d6aeef2b43d</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">35</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf</data><data key="quote">d PSV3 on all CPP hydraulic modules. • Implemented a maintenance programme in which at least PSV1, PSV3 and NRV6 are disabled and their function checked once every 5 years. • Added a full flow check-valve, with an opening pressure of 10-12 bar, in the return oil circuit by-passing PSV3, the Oil Cooler and NRV6. Also, an additional alarm signal was to be fitted in the control system to give an alarm</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fa8b800951e9a69b" source="shipkg:faulttype:6456485708ad" target="shipkg:action:acaa49cd0860"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:2bfc3c9a35fee950</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN039_marine_shaft_generators.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-039_C-Marine-Shaft-Generators.pdf</data><data key="quote">and will ensure that the coupling between gearbox and the shaft generator is a high quality, designed for purpose unit, which can absorb misalignment, and also torsional vibrations to help the generator remain reliable. POWER TAKE OUT (PTO) / POWER TAKE IN (PTI) / POWER TAKE HOME (PTH) Marine shaft generators are often required to operate in a multi-function role. They could o</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fad2b7fdbf57beee" source="shipkg:condition:db2e89c50479" target="shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:3bea0430b472030b</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">64</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">current imbalance transformer were tested during manufacture, subsequent tests of the system were by secondary current injection, bypassing the windings. As the IAS did not specifically register which rank of the HF had developed an imbalance current, it was not possible to confirm if the current imbalance transformers on rank 1 1.3 had ever worked in service. It is concerning th</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "fuel_air", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fae55111f22503c3" source="shipkg:faulttype:f8ea1aa17718" target="shipkg:symptom:986db6816df4"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:cooling_cavitation</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9b96e30fbe8114af</data><data key="source_file">MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf</data><data key="page">11</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf</data><data key="quote">a function of the engine load and the ambient conditions. When reducing the water flow the following implications are foreseen: – Increased scavenge air temperature which will lead to a reduction of the water condensation amount in certain ambient conditions. Reduced water condensation will lead to a higher humidity level in the combustion chamber, which will have a negative effect on the ge</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fb00168862e5f699" source="shipkg:case:537a034e93e3" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_03_turning_gear</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:b840391c6c40b9b8</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">16</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fb3714370d60b45b" source="shipkg:fault:7c36cc5888d4" target="shipkg:faulttype:12275851bbd1"><data key="relation">INSTANCE_OF</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:coupling_failure</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:d3e64cd30311c1bb</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2017_20_Hebrides_CPP_coupling.pdf</data><data key="page">35</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/59b7ab1c40f0b61231e71a54/MAIBInvReport20_2017.pdf</data><data key="quote">s caused by the loosening of a setscrew used to attach a coupling to a stepper motor shaft due to its lack of rundown torque, the absence of thread locking fluid, and vibration during the actuator’s operation. [2.2] 3. The absence of service instructions for the actuator’s inspection and maintenance that were available from its manufacturer was pivotal to the failure. [2.3] 4. No thread l</data><data key="name">归入故障类别</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_basis": "人工审核术语分类；不是由该文献证明所有实例根因相同", "name": "归入故障类别", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fbc1bc6eae5124a5" source="shipkg:faulttype:6dbd0d51366c" target="shipkg:fault:7dd3cdd4fe58"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:bearing_electrical_erosion</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0f7534e3f93d98e3</data><data key="source_file">STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="source_url">https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf</data><data key="quote">porting bearings, consequently any resulting current flow will pass across the rolling element of the bearings, and will initiate electrical erosion of the bearing materials, eventually reducing the low friction expectation of the bearing. It is possible for a single bearing alternator to suffer from shaft bearing currents, but here the current flow path at the drive end of the alternator’s shaft mus</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fbc5db279b3cf9d4" source="shipkg:consequence:81fff36694d8" target="shipkg:fault:34646312c70d"><data key="relation">PRECEDED</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_22_cooling_pipe</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:f99011c1bd987967</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">59</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">e bilge pump but could not reach the two sea water inlet valves as they were already more than a metre below the water level. The main engine then stopped and the engineer told the skipper that nothing could be done to stem the ingress of water. The Figure 1: Sequence showing fishing vessel sinking</data><data key="name">先于</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "先于", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fc333e45409b3219" source="shipkg:equipment:5d25f4bda048" target="shipkg:component:6f0aead2b5a6"><data key="relation">HAS_COMPONENT</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4f930aa49cf38734</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">ch went according to plan until the ferry was about 1½ ships’ length from its final berthing position, when her three main engine clutches disengaged almost simultaneously. No Air, No Clutch, No CPP , No Brakes Damage to lubrication oil pipe and bottom end bearing Bottom end bearing Failed lubricant oil pipe end fitting</data><data key="name">包含部件</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "包含部件", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fc8aac60ddb0a728" source="shipkg:faulttype:3353dce7f4ad" target="shipkg:condition:ef7365f4e337"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">knowledge:bearing_seizure</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a6b5f4147115c639</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2013_569_bearing_wear_monitoring.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2013-569.pdf</data><data key="quote">g wear monitoring (BWM) system as recommended by MAN Diesel &amp; Turbo (MDT). However, for reasons not relevant in this context, the crew did not react to the alarm and slow-down signals from the BWM system. Operation of the engine continued until the oil mist detec - tor (OMD) alarm set off and requested slow-down. At this stage, the bearing damage had evolved into a situation where compreh</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fce2cc0d319e4881" source="shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_08_generator_oil</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:7e21ab64015c1360</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">26</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fd16ad255f22091c" source="shipkg:case:551512d967af" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">IN_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_02_control_air</data><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:8b57dbab2f3af128</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres</data><data key="name">涉及子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fd3a7af3d7b6d40d" source="shipkg:condition:7da9174934f9" target="shipkg:fault:439f73a406a0"><data key="relation">CONTRIBUTED_TO</data><data key="case_id">sd2013_03_turning_gear</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:85dce6df90ffbd20</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">16</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">turning gear control lever with the intention of disengaging the turning gear from the main engine flywheel. The turning gear was not marked in any way to show whether it was engaged or disengaged, and the operating instructions that were posted nearby had been painted over. The engineer then went to the machinery control room to start the engine. Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control</data><data key="name">促成</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "促成", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": true}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fd4ddfffcf5bc874" source="shipkg:case:adf367a46f33" target="shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66"><data key="relation">IN_SYSTEM</data><data key="case_id">wight_sky_me2_2018</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4846a9af2b7e6456</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf</data><data key="page">84</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic</data><data key="name">采用动力架构</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "采用动力架构", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fdfcfa912161d0f0" source="shipkg:equipment:61cd855f5970" target="shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:0b7a42308cc8b6cc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf</data><data key="page">84</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">D OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silica sand and other abrasive particles embe</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "transmission", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fe66d3f252c52257" source="shipkg:case:597875e258c6" target="shipkg:action:2c60146dc1a8"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_05_cpp_backup</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:74d39332305ecab7</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">and rectified the problem. Engineers are put on standby in control rooms during manoeuvring operations for a reason; not least to keep the bridge team informed of the status of all safety-critical systems. 4. The vessel’s crew were all experienced and many of them had spent most of their career operating similar types of vessels with the same company. However, the bridge and engineering teams did not</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fe7ae1fd68f1211c" source="shipkg:fault:41a15c8ffad7" target="shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:4cdcbf4e0a149c7e</data><data key="source_file">MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="source_url">https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf</data><data key="quote">t in thermal overload of the components to be cooled by the engine cooling water. A thermal overload may, however, also result in cracks and leakages as seen in the exhaust valve seat ring. Insufficient cooling water flow has widespread consequenc - es, in many cases this will influence the combustion process as well and therefore the overall performance and safety of Fig. 1:</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "cooling", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fe9cd56fb06fbf29" source="shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56" target="shipkg:fault:5bc176965c58"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_08_generator_oil</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:a36fbb3ebb9e478c</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">26</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">t unlagged following its overhaul during the recent dry dock (Figure 2b). This was hidden from view by the exhaust casing. • Fine oil spray ignited when it came into contact with the hot exhaust casing. Figure 1: Location of the generator with the loose oil plug and the adjacent generator with the uninsulated section of the exhaust piping</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:fef8f4c4663670cd" source="shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b" target="shipkg:condition:b290b6459200"><data key="relation">INVOLVES</data><data key="case_id">sd2016_14_sea_valve</data><data key="certainty">reported</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9bfb29365e610d09</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf</data><data key="page">40</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">nected the electric motor from the pump. He then removed the flange bolts connecting the inlet pipe to the pump. Soon afterwards, water started to flow from the inlet pipe at a rapidly increasing rate. The chief engineer tried to reduce the rate by jamming rags into the pipe, but the flow was too strong. He then sent the motorman to fetch some pieces of wood, which he intended to force into the pip</data><data key="name">涉及</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "涉及", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ff2bc2e691b752a6" source="shipkg:fault:c8fa85d36573" target="shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:f17ab4bbdcec2bfc</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">13</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectri</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "electrical", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ff7e18df79deaa60" source="shipkg:action:04317a406bca" target="shipkg:fault:5737f3610967"><data key="relation">ADDRESSES</data><data key="case_id">queen_mary2_hf_2010</data><data key="certainty">reported_action</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:54970b12e1896794</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">70</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf</data><data key="quote">e of its capacitors and the circumstances that could lead to this. • Replaced the capacitors in QM2’s aft harmonic filter with an improved and safer design. • Carried out a quality audit of the capacitor manufacturer. Lloyd’s Register (Europe, Middle East and Asia) has: • Progressed with existing work to review its rules to recognise and mitigate the hazard of arc-flash associated w</data><data key="name">应对</data><data key="props_json">{"name": "应对", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ff8cce45e75fb388" source="shipkg:component:0dcadce61c82" target="shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:9c5f7101c8442b54</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf</data><data key="page">15</data><data key="source_url">https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf</data><data key="quote">essel was able to berth safely alongside, assisted by harbour tugs. Subsequent investigation identified that No2 compressor had a damaged discharge valve. Neither compressor had been able to keep up with demand.</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "fuel_air", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge><edge id="edge:ffd0b2d7d280b726" source="shipkg:condition:6fa538170906" target="shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46"><data key="relation">BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM</data><data key="case_id" /><data key="certainty">curated_classification</data><data key="evidence_id">ev:1b6ee0d38c733128</data><data key="source_file">MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf</data><data key="page">6</data><data key="source_url">https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan</data><data key="quote">edules are only applicable for these parts. Non-Caterpillar parts used in the engine tent to have a shorter service life. [sic] • Check the use of non-Caterpillar bearings in the other engines on the vessel. If so, plan a early change of the main and connecting rod bearings. [sic] Parts approval process The approval process for a ship’s engine parts involved several steps to ensure compliance with safety and performanc</data><data key="name">归属子系统</data><data key="props_json">{"classification_rule": "lubrication", "name": "归属子系统", "graph_version": "3.0", "is_causal": false}</data></edge></graph></graphml>